-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Decision functions answer `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "where", "if", "unless" or "after" not met).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer (a scope limit, a bare "must" not done, a list that is not closed, a lifted bar).
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer (the Court may order otherwise in the interests of justice).
-- Order 9, Rule 24 and the Civil Procedure Convention are not among the sources: what they say is an input.
-- This Order fixes no period, so no time is counted in it (O 3 r 3 plays no part).

§ `Order 55 -- Obtaining evidence for foreign courts, etc.`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- Jurisdiction of Registrar to make order (O. 55, r. 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 55 r 1(1) the kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `o 55 r 1(1) an order for the examination of witnesses`
    `o 55 r 1(1) an order for attendance`
    `o 55 r 1(1) an order for production of documents`
    `o 55 r 1(1) a direction`
    `o 55 r 1(1) another kind of order`

-- COVERS O 55 r 1(1)
-- src:6705 | 1. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), the power of the General Division or a Judge sitting in the General Division to make, in relation to a matter pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside the jurisdiction, orders for the examination of witnesses and for attendance and for production of documents and to give directions, may be exercised by the Registrar. (2) The Registrar may not make such an order if the matter in question is a criminal matter.
@ref O 55 r 1(1) (src:6705)
GIVEN `the matter is pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter in question is a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `o 55 r 1(1) the kind of order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 55 r 1(1) the Registrar may exercise the power to make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the matter is pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside the jurisdiction`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "in relation to a matter pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside the jurisdiction"
        IF `the matter in question is a criminal matter`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (2)", and paragraph (2) says "The Registrar may not make such an order if the matter in question is a criminal matter"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 55 r 1(1) another kind of order`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "orders for the examination of witnesses and for attendance and for production of documents and to give directions"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Paragraph (2): a bar that applies "if the matter in question is a criminal matter".  Where the bar is not engaged it grants nothing.
-- COVERS O 55 r 1(2)
-- src:6705 | 1. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), the power of the General Division or a Judge sitting in the General Division to make, in relation to a matter pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside the jurisdiction, orders for the examination of witnesses and for attendance and for production of documents and to give directions, may be exercised by the Registrar. (2) The Registrar may not make such an order if the matter in question is a criminal matter.
@ref O 55 r 1(2) (src:6705)
GIVEN `it is an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter in question is a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 55 r 1(2) the Registrar is barred from making the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it is an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "such an order"
        IF `the matter in question is a criminal matter`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the matter in question is a criminal matter" is an "if" condition

-- COVERS O 55 r 1(2)
-- JUDGMENT QA | O 55 r 1(2) | `o 55 r 1(2) the Registrar may make the order` | NOTHING when the matter is not a criminal matter (a bar that is not engaged grants nothing; the permission comes from paragraph (1)); the twin `o 55 r 1(2) the Registrar is barred from making the order` answers JUST FALSE | JUST TRUE (the matter not being criminal permits it)
@ref O 55 r 1(2) (src:6705)
GIVEN `it is an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter in question is a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 55 r 1(2) the Registrar may make the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 55 r 1(2) the Registrar is barred from making the order` `it is an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` `the matter in question is a criminal matter`
    WHEN JUST barred THEN
        IF barred
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may not make such an order if the matter in question is a criminal matter"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the bar is not engaged and grants nothing
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar does not reach this order

